+/* ---- Patch 0080: cellGcm_skip_ticks(n) -- give up exactly n frames.
+ *
+ * The next n vblank ticks that would complete a flip are skipped: no vblank,
+ * no flip completion, no handlers. The frame in flight stays on the screen one
+ * refresh longer (it was presented when translated) and the game's next frame
+ * starts one tick later; the ticks after it keep the display's grid. A game
+ * that has to slow down by a frame (rollback time sync, T5DR's
+ * src/rollback/rb_net.cpp) cannot do it any other way: holding its frame start
+ * past a tick makes PS3_LATE_FLIP (patch 0059) hold the next tick for a frame
+ * that is late on purpose, and the frame was given up twice (two ticks) or, a
+ * tick that came during the wait having been counted, not at all. Timing only:
+ * the game runs the same frames. */
+static std::atomic<int> g_skip_ticks{ 0 };
+extern "C" void cellGcm_skip_ticks(int n) { if (n > 0) g_skip_ticks.fetch_add(n); }
